{"packet_id":"D073-02","doc_id":"D073","jurisdiction":"San Diego, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"No-fault just cause termination notice and relocation assistance","requirement":"A landlord terminating a tenancy for no-fault just cause must give 30- or 60-day written notice stating the basis, the tenant's relocation assistance (two months' rent, or three months for a senior or disabled tenant, or a rent waiver), and the renewal-offer right.","key_value":"2 months' rent; 3 months if senior or disabled","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental properties subject to Division 7; relocation assistance applies regardless of the tenant's income or length of tenancy, and a senior or disabled tenant receives three months' rent.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential rental property subject to Division 7"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Failure to strictly comply renders any termination notice void; failure to provide relocation assistance makes the landlord liable for not less than three times the required relocation assistance and actual damages; wrongful eviction damages of not less than three times actual economic damages.","effective_date":"2023-06-24","citation":"San Diego Mun. Code § 98.0706","quoted_span":"(i) Unless section 98.0706(c)(1)(A)(ii) applies, the direct payment to the tenant shall be in an amount equal to two months of actual rent under the tenant’s lease in effect at the date of the notice. (ii) If the tenant is a senior or disabled, the direct payment to the tenant shall be in an amount equal to three months of actual rent under the tenant’s lease in effect at the date of the notice.","interaction":"Relocation assistance is credited against any other relocation assistance required by any federal, state, or other local law.","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D073-02","doc_id":"D073","jurisdiction":"San Diego, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Buyout agreement requirements and void buyouts","requirement":"Before making a buyout offer, a landlord must give each tenant a written disclosure of the tenant's rights; any buyout agreement for less than the relocation assistance owed to the tenant is void.","key_value":"Buyout amount must be greater than relocation assistance owed","coverage_conditions":"Buyout offers and agreements with tenants of residential rental properties subject to Division 7.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential rental property subject to Division 7"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"A buyout agreement that does not strictly comply with the section, or is for less than the relocation assistance owed, is void; rights under the section may not be waived.","effective_date":"2023-06-24","citation":"San Diego Mun. Code § 98.0707","quoted_span":"Buyout agreements must be for an amount that is greater than the amount of relocation assistance available to the tenant in section 98.0706(c). A buyout agreement for less than the amount of relocation assistance owed to the tenant violates this Division and is void.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
